  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Area Approximations: building the trapezoidal rule from trapezia</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.2 (b) / Essential 2.1 (b): Write the area of one strip as a trapezium in terms of ordinates, then add the areas of all the strips and collect the terms to obtain the trapezoidal rule.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Section C of Chapter 9 (the trapezium areas collected to the short cut) of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: n strips with a numeric strip width and ordinates y0 to yn; randomised strip and named feedback for each slip.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
